  "rationale": "TWIN CONTRACT. dym-transform and dym-transform-partial are byte-identical apart from the `promotion` DOMAIN_PROBE entry (and two comment rules), so every behaviour that is not promotion-specific MUST hold identically on both. Ported deliberately rather than left to the twin: this repo has been bitten before by a fork asserted to be identical that had quietly drifted, and a rule proven on only one copy is a rule the other copy is free to lose. Same inputs, same expected output as dym-transform/HC-cap3-per-token-then-five-token-slice.json \u2014 if the two ever disagree, one of these two fixtures fails.\n\nBehaviour under test: Two independent bounds compose: cap3 keeps each token to three candidates and the token list itself is sliced to five. Six missed tokens with one candidate each therefore probe exactly five codes \u2014 under product_attachment's cap of 8, so the token slice is what is being measured here rather than the probe cap.",
